    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Disability-competent care at every visit: introductions and spoken orientation, describing each step of the examination, offering an arm for guiding, and all documents in an accessible electronic format. Guideline: Vision Rehabilitation Preferred Practice Pattern (2023) [S]</item><item>Ophthalmology consultation to examine the blind eyes for comfort and complications and to advise on pressure checks and surveillance. Guideline: Primary Open-Angle Glaucoma Preferred Practice Pattern (2025); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, glaucoma and depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monographs (2026) [S]</item><item>Recovery-oriented care: ask about cravings, triggers, and any return to use at each visit in a non-judgmental way; naloxone at home and when traveling; recovery supports he can reach; and a written plan for any future pain. Guideline: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Substance Use Disorders (2021); The ASAM National Practice Guideline for the Treatment of Opioid Use Disorder: 2020 Focused Update (2020) [S]</item><item>Depression screening with the PHQ-9 at intake and at six months, PHQ-2 at the wellness visit, and a safety review with the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline at each visit. Guideline: Depression and Suicide Risk in Adults: Screening (2023); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, glaucoma and depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monographs (2026) [S]</item><item>Medicine labeling: audio labels from the pharmacy, a braille label on the naloxone, and the same pharmacy for every prescription. Guideline: Vision Rehabilitation Preferred Practice Pattern (2023) [S]</item><item>Fall prevention: CDC STEADI screen at each visit, keeping the home layout unchanged, and a sighted guide in unfamiliar places. Guideline: Vision Rehabilitation Preferred Practice Pattern (2023) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
